tunities for student and scientific communities.\nKey figures\n260\nResearchers and professors\n200\nStudents in Master's programs\n10\nLaboratories\n200\nPhD students\nSubjects\nTheoretical physics and its applications\nQuantum physics\nWave physics\nSoft matter\nBiophysics\nNonlinear physics and Hydrodynamics\nPHD Track\nPSL PhD tracks | Join outstanding students from around the globe and launch your world-class research career with the PSL Graduate programme\nThe highly selective PhD tracks at PSL University prepare students for research careers in France or abroad, in academia or industry.\nThese five-year programmes are designed for high-potential students who want to tackle the scientific challenges of tomorrow and prepare their research project from the Master's level onwards. Immersed in the ecosystem of excellence of the PSL Physics graduate programme (top-level laboratories and academic teams, international partners), successful applicants benefit from a personalised course of study geared towards their thesis topic from the first year of their Master's degree.\nWhy join the PSL PhD track?\nCurriculum of excellence (Master's + PhD) accessible in M1\nFunding for the entire duration of studies (5 years) & welcome package in year 1\nCourses taught entirely in English\nClose supervision & support for professional integration\nImmersion in a multicultural & cutting-edge scientific environment in the heart of Paris\nFind out more (admissions, scholarships, etc.)\nDiscover the PhD track & apply\nEductation\nResearch\nChoose your Master\u2019s degree and define your academic path\nThe graduate program offers the following Master\u2019s degrees:\nMaster's degree in Physics\nMaster's degree in Quantum Engineering\nPersonalized course offerings\nComplementary university-wide courses\nGraduate program students at both the Master\u2019s and PhD level have access to university-wide trainings in core competencies, both introductory and advanced, designed to supplement their academic study.\nThose complementary university-wide courses, available in all of PSL\u2019s component schools, are eligible for ECTS credit.\nCentre de langues\nPSL Weeks\nMineures certifiantes\nEntrepreneuriat\nData science program\nData science program\nParis School of IA\nInstitute of Public Action\nPariSant\u00e9 Campus\nCareer opportunities\nTrained in and through research, PSL alumni find numerous employment opportunities in the public, private and entrepreneurial sectors as well as in the academic world.\nPursue a PhD\nDoctoral research is conducted in a PSL laboratory. Training is conducted in a doctoral school.\nGraduate program doctoral schools\n\u00c9cole doctorale Physique en Ile-de-France - ED 564\nGraduate program laboratories\nGulliver\nESPCI Paris - PSL (UMR 7083)\nInstitut Langevin\nESPCI Paris - PSL (UMR 7587)\nLaboratoire Kastler Brossel - LKB\nENS - PSL (UMR 8552)\nLaboratoire de Physique et d'Etude des Mat\u00e9riaux - LPEM\nESPCI Paris - PSL (UMR 8213)\nLaboratoire Physico-Chimie Curie - PCC\nInstitut Curie (UMR 168)\nLaboratoire de Physique de l'ENS - PSL\nENS - PSL (UMR 8023)\nLaboratoire Univers et Th\u00e9ories - LUTH\nObservatoire de Paris - PSL (UMR 8102)\nPhysique et M\u00e9canique des Milieux H\u00e9t\u00e9rog\u00e8nes\nESPCI Paris - PSL (UMR 7636)\nSciences et Ing\u00e9nierie de la Mati\u00e8re Molle - SIMM\nESPCI Paris - PSL (UMR 7615)\nSYRTE\nObservatoire de Paris - PSL (UMR 8630)\nContact\nHead of the Graduate program:\nGiulio Biroli (ENS - PSL)\nLuca de'Medici (ESPCI-PSL)\ngp-physics@psl.eu\nPSL Phd tracks\nPSL Sport\nAll you need to know about sports at PSL\nAthletics at PSL\nPSL Explore\nGateway to knowledge dissemination and digital collections\nRead more\nMain navigation\nUniversity\nAbout us\nSchools\nInternational rankings\nOrganization\nNews\nPariSant\u00e9 Campus\nInvestments for the Future Program\nMedia Relations and Communications\nJoin us\nThe PSL Foundation\nEducation\nFind your curriculum\nAdmissions\nPSL voices 